\n- Y-axis uses a logarithmic scale with ticks at approximately 1, 10, 100, 1000, and 10000.\n- Bars are ordered from highest to lowest count and colored with a red-to-blue gradient.\n\nBiological/source objects:\n- Disease categories from MeSH.\n- Gene-disease associations, likely counts of associations between genes and diseases grouped by category.\n\nDisease categories shown include:\n- Neoplasms\n- Congenital abnormality\n- Digestive system diseases\n- Nervous system diseases\n- Cardiovascular diseases\n- Urologic and male genital diseases\n- Skin disease\n- Mental disorders\n- Metabolic diseases\n- Endocrine system diseases\n- Pathology\n- Immune system diseases\n- Musculoskeletal diseases\n- Respiratory tract diseases\n- Hemic and lymphatic diseases\n- Eye diseases\n- Bacterial infections and mycoses\n- Chemically induced disorders\n- Stomatognathic diseases\n- Otorhinolaryngologic diseases\n- Behavior and behavior mechanisms\n- Animal diseases\n- Wounds and injuries\n- Occupational diseases\n- Disorders of environmental origin\n- Psychological phenomena and processes\n\nVisible finding:\n- Neoplasms have the highest number of gene-disease associations, above 10,000.\n- Most major disease categories have hundreds to several thousand associations.\n- “Disorders of environmental origin” and “Psychological phenomena and processes” have the fewest associations, near the bottom of the logarithmic scale.\n\nNo multi-panel layout, biological microscopy images, molecular structures, workflow transformations, or model interface diagrams are visible."]}, {"figure_index": 18, "page_no": 22, "caption": "", "vlm_descriptions": ["SCIENTIFIC_FIGURE\n\nThe image is a multi-panel bar-chart figure comparing model performance metrics.\n\nVisible panels:\n- Top left: `Accuracy`\n- Top middle: `Recall`\n- Top right: `Specificity`\n- Bottom left: `F1 Score`\n- Bottom middle: `MCC`\n\nLabels/models shown along x-axes include:\n`Xunzi-R`, `o3`, `GPT-5`, `DeepSeek-R1`, `DeepSeek-V3`,